[15.254002, "o", "# acme-app\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n- **Archetype:** fullstack\r\n- **Language / runtime:** python (), pkg: uv\r\n- **Framework / architecture:** next / layered\r\n\r\nThis file is the entry point Claude Code reads on every turn. It is deliberately\r\na **lean pointer**, not a knowledge dump: it tells Claude *where the truth lives*\r\nand *how to work here*, then gets out of the way. The truth lives in the **specs**\r\n(narrative Markdown) and the **contracts** (the approval oracle). Read the spec\r\nbefore you write code — in this project, **specs lead and code follows**.\r\n\r\n## How to work here\r\n\r\n1. **Read the spec first.** The `specs/` documents below are the source of intent.\r\n   Before implementing anything, read the relevant spec section; if it is empty or\r\n   stale, fill it (or run `/ack-spec`) *before* writing code — never the reverse.\r\n"]
[15.254073, "o", "2. **Least code.** Prefer the smallest change that satisfies the spec. Do not add\r\n"]
